Sonata address map: a third TL-UL host, the CHERIoT revocation engine

Local, uncommitted change in the sonata-system checkout this was vendored from (the Sonata
integration of the OpenTitan CHERIoT memory subsystem adds the TRBE as a crossbar host). The RTOS
test SoC uses only this package's ADDR_SPACE_* / ADDR_MASK_* constants, so the change has no effect
here; it is kept so the vendored file is the one the flow was validated with.

diff --git a/rtl/bus/tl_main_pkg.sv b/rtl/bus/tl_main_pkg.sv
index 2371e71..d6650b2 100644
--- a/rtl/bus/tl_main_pkg.sv
+++ b/rtl/bus/tl_main_pkg.sv
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ package tl_main_pkg;
   localparam logic [31:0] ADDR_MASK_DBG_DEV     = 32'h 00000fff;
   localparam logic [31:0] ADDR_MASK_RV_PLIC     = 32'h 07ffffff;
 
-  localparam int N_HOST   = 2;
+  localparam int N_HOST   = 3;
   localparam int N_DEVICE = 24;
 
   typedef enum int {
@@ -88,7 +88,8 @@ package tl_main_pkg;
 
   typedef enum int {
     TlIbexLsu = 0,
-    TlDbgHost = 1
+    TlDbgHost = 1,
+    TlCheriotTrbe = 2
